WEBVTT

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.950
Karin!

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.660
Karin! Hey!

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.160
Karin! Can you hear me?

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.670
Karin! Are you okay?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.210
Karin! Hey!

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.010
What's the big idea, you old bag?!
Show yourself!

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.130
Where'd you go?!
Fight me!

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.720
Hey! Let's see you
try that again!

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.550
Any ideas, Yukimaru?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.550
Fight me!

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.110
And with that, Colonel, the White Marginal
has been delivered as promised.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.240
- What reward can I expect this time—
- Get out.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.530
Huh?

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.870
I thought I told you
she was to be unharmed.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.500
- Those scratches hardly count as—
- Did you not hear me?

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.130
Get. Out.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.260
Sis? Wait for me!
Sis, are you listening?

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.760
- Stand aside, you wooden-headed lubber!
- Stand aside!

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.160
I beg your forgiveness. It would appear that
my orders were not sufficiently clear.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.040
I had no intention
of causing you harm.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.540
You're lovely.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.380
Er, I'm sorry...
I'm a little confused...

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.550
We meet at last,

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.420
...Fena Houtman.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.050
I've been searching for you
for ten long years,

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:49.350
...my princess.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.020
<b>No luck here.</b>

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.150
Crap!

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.650
If we'd known this was gonna happen,
we should've killed 'em in Bar-Baral!

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:38.280
We don't harm women
or children.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.990
That's the rule,
so what else could we do?

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:43.620
Hey, now! Is this okay?
Is it cute? Do I look cute?

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.290
- Be honest!
- I-I think you look cute.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.000
- Do I? You aren't lying, are you?
- Sure...

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.040
- Why did you look away just now?
- I didn't look away.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.510
What is Yukimaru doing?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.880
Looking for explosives.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:03.180
If you set off a mishmash of charges
like that, some always fail to go off.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.140
There's a crack in the ceiling.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.150
We're beneath the river.
Water is heavy.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.270
If an explosion goes off in here,
nature will take its course.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.650
Oh, I follow you.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.950
And we also have two monkeys
capable of climbing up there.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.450
"Two monkeys"

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.450
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.740
Okay, Shitan.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.320
This.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:25.830
You're the same pygmy you've
always been. Nothing has changed.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.460
Let's see how you like it!

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:29.960
Shitan.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.460
Found one.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:05.200
N-Now what?!

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.340
Hey! Are you guys okay?

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.340
What happened in there?!

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.400
If its aroma isn't to your liking,
I can brew something else.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:43.360
N-No, the tea is fine.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:49.120
- Look, I—
- La Pucelle.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:51.870
H-How do you know that word?

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.750
I knew your honored mother.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.000
"Honored mother"?

00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:59.920
You knew my mother?

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.510
She was a lovely person.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.760
Eyes of a deep blue
like that of the South Seas.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.770
White skin more beautiful
than freshly-fallen snow.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:13.640
Platinum hair that would shine
like burnished steel.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.020
A smile that would bring happiness
to all who met her.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:22.990
You truly are
the very image of her.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.330
I... I don't know anything
about my mother.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.540
Yes, I know.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:34.670
I hope there will come a time when I will
be able to tell you all about her.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:38.500
But there is something else
that I must inform you of first.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.550
Do you know who they really are?

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.720
Who "they" are?
You mean Yukimaru and the others?

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.560
"The goblins will come
to snatch you away..."

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.560
Have you heard that before?

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.350
I've... heard it.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.400
They kill women and children
without hesitation.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.940
Where they have passed by,
nothing but poppies grow.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.240
Devils who came from the East.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.950
Murderers who drift
wherever the wind takes them.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.950
When I was young, I, too,
was told stories about them.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.580
Those tales are no mere legend.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.460
The Goblin Knights actually exist.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.210
Fena, you

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.970
...have been living under the
same roof as those devils.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.230
Where do you think you're going?

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:43.280
- We're gonna rescue Fena!
- We don't have time to relax!

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.400
Forget it!

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:46.740
Karin. You memorized
those numbers, I take it?

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.740
Yeah, sure.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:54.450
"Upon obtaining either the coordinates
or a map, return at once."

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.750
Those are our orders from Yukihisa.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:57.790
Huh?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.790
I thought our job
was to protect Fena!

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:04.250
Or isn't it?

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:10.340
Our ancestors were given a vital mission
by the Imperial Court of the day

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.260
and set out from our homeland.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:17.270
They are searching for a legendary treasure
that was hidden centuries ago.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:20.270
A legendary treasure?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:23.770
It's a mythical treasure that was snuck out
of the country at the end of the 3rd Century

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.480
and hidden somewhere.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:28.280
It's said to be capable
of founding a nation.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.450
One of Japan's three
sacred treasures, long since lost.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.200
The sword Kusanagi.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:38.250
"Locate it using any means necessary
and bring it back home."

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:43.790
That is the sacred mission
that was entrusted to our clan.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:48.130
And as for the place
where the sword lies hidden,

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.300
its name is...

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:50.930
- ...Eden.
- Eden.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.930
<i>Go to Eden!</i>

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.890
A lost land
that the powers that be

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:59.310
have frantically searched for
over the centuries.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:03.770
A vast temple which conceals a treasure
that can rule the world.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.820
There are some who call it
the Vault of the Earth.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:11.490
In short, the treasures spoken of
in legends from around the globe

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.320
all lie hidden in this place.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.660
That is what Eden is.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.620
"In Eden, King Solomon
lies sleeping.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.170
Three paces to the king's left,

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:23.130
he concealed the blade
of the gods."

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.960
That report came from Yajiro
during his travels with Xavier.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.090
So Eden is where we begin.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.090
Our first order of business
is to reach it.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.350
And then there are the Houtmans,
a bloodline with deep ties to Eden.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:39.140
Hey, wait a minute!

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:41.980
You're saying the reason
we've served the Houtmans is—

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:44.770
The shipwreck was an accident.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:47.230
But over the course of
serving the Houtmans,

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.990
we learned that they had some
sort of connection to Eden.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:54.030
And then came the <i>Hope</i> incident
ten years ago.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:57.280
Franz shouted it out
in front of Fena and Yukimaru:

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.500
"Go to Eden!"

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.460
Franz is no longer with us.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.000
The only clues we have left
that might lead us to Eden

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:10.260
lie hidden in Fena's memories.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.760
You are being used by them
to serve their ends.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:17.850
You're wrong! F-For one thing,
Yukimaru saved my life!

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:19.260
That's because

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.640
...he learned that you are the key
to their reaching Eden.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:25.730
Saved your life?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.730
They cut you, a mere child,
adrift into a stormy sea.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:34.240
It wasn't your life that was
of vital importance to them.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:39.200
They only did it because they feared Fena Houtman
falling into the hands of their enemies.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.210
That's not true!

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.710
Princess Fena.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:52.090
The thing about the truth... It is never
the ideal we pictured in our heads.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.890
Who gives a damn about that?!

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.890
I don't care about her memories!

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:02.020
Doesn't that just mean that Yukihisa's
been lying to us all this time?

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:03.930
Fena would never lie to us!

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:04.850
Yeah! What he said!

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:08.110
Shitan, we can't just
turn our backs on Fena.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:11.230
She is one of us now.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:12.990
Let's go rescue her.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.860
There's no time for that.

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:18.620
I've reported that we have
obtained the coordinates.

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.870
If we don't return to the island now,
we would be breaking the law.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:22.870
That's just a formality!

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.960
- We'll just not tell them, same as—
- We can't!

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.620
He's... on his way.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:28.540
Huh?

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:29.880
We didn't catch that!

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.760
Kei is on his way here.

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.140
Why... would he send Kei?

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:52.520
He's not...

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.530
He's not coming to <i>kill</i> us, is he?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.450
Think it through.

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:00.240
If we let our emotions get the better of us
and we go off to rescue Fena,

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:03.330
we'll be seen as rebels
who disobeyed a direct order.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.830
In other words, we would
become fugitives.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.330
You know what happens
to such people.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:13.340
We'll be hunted to the ends
of the earth and executed.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:21.050
We have no other choice
but to return to the island.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:23.850
Yukimaru, wait!

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.350
Yukimaru!

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:31.650
- Let's head back for now!
- Yeah! Then we can get Yukihisa's blessing!

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:33.360
We'll still have time
to save her!

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.360
The rest of you,
go back to the island.

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:39.660
No one else needs
to be a fugitive.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.370
Don't be stupid!

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:44.950
How many people do you think you'll be
going up against?! That's a pirate ship!

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.950
If you go in alone,
you'd be committing suicide!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.620
And even if you manage to
get her out, Kei would—

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:56.380
Don't go.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:58.970
Fena is a witch.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:01.550
She steals the heart
of everyone she meets.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.220
And she leads all those
she's bewitched to their doom.

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:07.390
Yukimaru.
Come to your senses.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.480
Let's all go back to the island.

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:16.900
For ten long years...

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.070
...I could never
get it out of my head.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:24.330
Her voice, shouting out my name
amid all the fire and terror.

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.200
Her trembling hand.

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:29.290
Her eyes, filled with despair
and sadness as she drifted away.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:31.920
The emptiness that descended
on me afterwards.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.130
I'll never let go of her hand again.

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:38.420
It doesn't matter to me
who she is.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.300
I'm going to go save Fena.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:45.430
If anyone tries to get in my way,
no matter who they are,

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.100
I'll kill them without mercy!

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.400
Should we have let him go?

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.580
Guys...

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.170
Yukimaru...

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.130
Y-Yes?

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.590
Pardon the intrusion.
I've brought a change of clothes.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.350
Er, um...

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.480
I'll leave them here.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.100
Hey, wait a minute!

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.310
- Yes?
- Are you busy?

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.320
Can we talk? I've been dying
to have someone to talk to.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.110
- I don't have time to—
- Sit over there!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.860
- C'mon, hurry!
- Fine...

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:07.240
What's your name?

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:11.740
Our paths have finally crossed...

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:16.080
I had an appointed task
as well, Helena.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:20.540
At long last, I will
be able to see you.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:34.540
Pirate Ship: Rumble Rose

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.020
Sis, got a minute?

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:45.530
- I'm busy. Go away.
- "Busy," my butt.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.410
The White Marginal
had this around her neck.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.870
Mind if I keep it?
It's kinda cute, don't you think?

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.670
- What's your name?
- It's Cody.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:08.510
- You don't strike me as a soldier.
- I'm here through the kindness of Lord Abel.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.680
His kindness?

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.720
I was born the child of a slave
on a Maxiver plantation.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.470
Hang on, you mean
that spoiled rich kid?

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.730
When I was five, I was sold
to a brothel on Shangri La,

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:24.230
and Lord Abel saved me
from a fate of working there.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:26.070
You lived on Shangri La?

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.070
- I was there, too!
- I'm well aware.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.070
- Why?
- This may be none of my business,

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.240
but it's impossible

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:35.830
to obtain both blue water
and storm clouds.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:41.750
<i>Which wilt thou choose?
Blue water? Or storm clouds?</i>

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:45.840
If what you want
is the truth,

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.010
there is only one path
for you to choose.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.650
Is that little girl
in that cabin?

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.690
Please turn around
and leave.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:08.400
This is a ship,
but it is English territory.

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:11.030
We can't have you roaming around
without permission.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.240
Stand aside!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.540
I said to stand aside, runt.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:23.710
No, <i>you</i> stand aside.
Go back to your own filthy ship.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.540
You don't deserve
to set foot on this one.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.300
Cody?!

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.810
Where did you get
your grubby mitts on this?

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:45.060
This is a pendant
that I gave to Abel.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.560
Wait, that's—

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.570
Little girl, how far back
do you and Abel go?

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.580
- Answer me!
- Stop... Keep your hands off—

00:18:58.910 --> 00:18:59.950
Cody!

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.750
Stupid kid.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.710
Why is Abel so obsessed
with you?

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:06.630
What are you scheming?

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:10.210
If you don't want to get hurt, you'd better
come clean to me about everything.

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:14.470
I don't... I don't have
anything to say to you!

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.260
Nothing at all—

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.770
I don't think you're
taking me seriously.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.230
All right.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.520
Let's see how tough
you really are.

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:32.150
Let... Let me go!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.880
You don't have the guts to—

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.760
I think you already
know this,

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.920
but hiding behind her
won't do you any good.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:59.510
At this distance, I can shoot
the wings off a fly.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.350
You have until the count of three
to release her.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.310
One.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.440
Two.

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:10.940
Three—

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.580
Abel?

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.710
A-Abel...

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.600
It's not El Dorado
that those coordinates

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:51.610
point the way to, is it?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:56.110
Get out of my sight.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.790
Sis?

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.670
Are you sure?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.250
We have the coordinates.

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:19.760
But isn't it supposed to be impossible
to reach them without that girl?

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.100
Sis! Are we just gonna run away
with our tail between our legs?!

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:25.350
- To hell with that!
- Sis!

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:30.520
Hard to port!
Stand ready on the cannons!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.920
Helena des Armoises.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:55.920
This is

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.300
...your mother.
